# Astra Z2 — practical weighing recipe

Date: 2026-09-06. Design: **PLI-ZERO-ASTRA-Z2**, Prada L'Homme Intense-inspired iris / sandalwood / patchouli / tonka. This is a practical view of the already selected Z2 composition, **not a new formula or dose revision**.

**One complete fragrance blend. All ingredient transfers below are grams of the named stock, not millilitres, microlitres or drops.** Use a calibrated balance with 0.001 g readability and verified accuracy at the smallest transfer, 0.040 g. If your balance cannot reliably weigh that amount, do not round the formula to fit the balance.

**Experimental preparation only.** Recipe arithmetic is not safety approval. Confirm stock labels and the applicable supplier SDS/handling instructions before handling. The three working solutions below must be completely dissolved and homogeneous before dosing. Skin use, gifting/sale and physical release remain HOLD pending an appropriate finished-product safety assessment; sensory performance and stability are unverified. IFRA limits concern the finished product, and conformity is not a replacement for safety assessment. [IFRA guidance](https://ifrafragrance.org/using-the-standards)

## 1. Prepare and label three working solutions

Prepare each in its own clean, compatible, capped vial. The quantities below make stock solutions, **not additional perfume test variants**. Do not pour the entire prepared stock into the perfume: use only the amounts in section 2.

| Label | Starting material g | DEP g | Total stock g | Mass basis |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Z2-ORI-10-DEP | 0.100 Orivone, neat | 0.900 | 1.000 | 10% w/w |
| Z2-HEL-10-DEP | 0.100 Heliotropal / piperonal, neat | 0.900 | 1.000 | 10% w/w |
| Z2-COU-20-DEP | 0.200 Coumarin, neat powder | 0.800 | 1.000 | 20% w/w |

The Coumarin preparation is a one-fifth-scale version of the selected formula's 1.000 g + 4.000 g preparation specification. Its mass fraction, carrier and amount dosed into the perfume are unchanged. Do not substitute the existing unspecified-basis Coumarin 20% DEP bottle or the approximately 25–30% saturated DPG stock. Use neat piperonal, not Heliotropin Fleuressence.

Mix at room temperature, keeping the vials closed between mixing. No dissolution time or solubility at these strengths is guaranteed. If crystals, sediment or separate layers remain, **do not dose the liquid above them, add extra solvent, or heat to force this recipe through**. Stop at that stock and resolve its preparation first. Label material, carrier, w/w strength, date and actual preparation masses; keep unused stock separately. These new solutions remain NOT PREPARED in the repository until the user actually makes and confirms them.

## 2. Weigh the complete 6.500 g concentrate

Start with a clean, dry, capped mixing vial of adequate capacity. Tare before every addition and add the amount in the **Add stock g** column, recording the actual transferred mass. Finish each basket before moving to the next. The existing basket order is retained, with descending **mass** within baskets; descending physical volume cannot be established without stock densities. Basket 7 for Linalyl Acetate is provisional. The separate DEP bottle location is not asserted.

| Basket | Material | Exact stock to use | Add stock g | Supplied product ppm w/w in concentrate |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|
| 1 | Ambrox Super | 25% w/w in DPG + IPM + ethanol; existing 3 + 7 + 0.5 + 1.5 g preparation | 0.560 | 21538.46 |
| 1 | Iso E Super | Neat / as supplied | 0.380 | 58461.54 |
| 1 | Hedione | Normal Hedione, neat; not Hedione HC | 0.360 | 55384.62 |
| 1 | Patchouli EO | Current owned neat / as-supplied stock | 0.260 | 40000.00 |
| 1 | Hexyl Salicylate | Neat / as supplied | 0.140 | 21538.46 |
| 3 | Sandalore | Neat / as supplied | 0.440 | 67692.31 |
| 3 | Cedarwood oil Virginia | Neat / as supplied; not another cedarwood | 0.140 | 21538.46 |
| 3 | Ebanol | Neat / as supplied | 0.060 | 9230.77 |
| 6 | Romandolide | Neat / as supplied | 0.200 | 30769.23 |
| 7* | Linalyl Acetate | Neat / as supplied | 0.040 | 6153.85 |
| 11 | Alpha-Isomethyl Ionone | Owned Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure), neat | 1.272 | 195692.31 |
| 11 | Alpha Irone | Existing 10% w/w in DEP | 0.400 | 6153.85 |
| 11 | Orivone | Newly prepared Z2-ORI-10-DEP, 10% w/w | 0.200 | 3076.92 |
| 11 | Dihydro Beta Ionone | Neat / as supplied | 0.160 | 24615.38 |
| 11 | Heliotropal | Newly prepared Z2-HEL-10-DEP, 10% w/w | 0.080 | 1230.77 |
| 12 | Tonkarome | Existing 20% w/w in TEC, made from 4 g product + 16 g TEC | 0.900 | 27692.31 |
| 12 | Coumarin | Newly prepared Z2-COU-20-DEP, 20% w/w | 0.800 | 24615.38 |
| Carrier | Diethyl Phthalate (DEP) | Neat / as supplied; separate carrier addition | 0.108 | 0.00 |
| | **TOTAL** | | **6.500** | **615384.62** |

**Do not omit the final 0.108 g DEP addition, and do not add the DEP from section 1 a second time.** The concentrate contains 4.000 g of supplied fragrant products and 2.500 g of known external carriers. Proprietary bases and natural oils are whole supplied products, not assayed pure molecules.

Known carrier accounting: DEP 1.360 g; TEC 0.720 g; DPG 0.326666667 g; IPM 0.023333333 g; ethanol 0.070 g. The small ethanol contribution already present in Ambrox Super stock is not the final bottle diluent.

Use the exact owned Tonkarome working bottle; no Firmenich-versus-Synarome substitution or internal coumarin fraction is inferred. Likewise, do not substitute the separate unresolved Givaudan AIMI entry for the specified Methyl Ionone Pure stock.

Cap and mix gently until homogeneous. Do not rinse material from transfer tools into the concentrate with extra solvent. Record errors rather than compensating by changing unrelated ingredient doses. No separate iris, wood, tonka or musk accords need to be compounded or evaluated.

## 3. Finish one measured 30.00 mL bottle

This preserves the selected formula's concentration definition: **6.00 mL of the complete homogeneous raw-stock concentrate in 30.00 mL final solution (20% v/v raw-stock concentrate)**. It is not a 20% w/w recipe or 20% pure odorants.

1. Check that the concentrate is completely homogeneous at room temperature. Using suitable calibrated volume-measuring equipment, measure **6.00 mL** of it into a clean finishing vessel. Record the transferred concentrate mass as well if finished ppm is needed.
2. Add the owned ethanol only if its label/SDS establishes that it is suitable for perfumery use. Add less than the final required amount first; mix, let bubbles settle and return to room temperature.
3. Add further ethanol **until the total mixed solution measures 30.00 mL**, then mix again. The final-volume mark belongs to the calibrated measuring vessel, not an assumed commercial bottle capacity. Do not simply add 24.00 mL of alcohol and assume volumes are perfectly additive.
4. Transfer to a clean, labeled, compatible tightly closing bottle. Label: "Astra Z2 / PLI-ZERO-ASTRA-Z2 — experimental; 20% v/v raw-stock concentrate; not cleared for skin use", preparation date and batch record. Keep any remaining concentrate labeled separately.

**6.500 g is not assumed to equal 6.00 mL.** If this master does not yield a measured 6.00 mL, make additional concentrate by scaling every section-2 mass by the same factor and homogenize before taking the aliquot. Do not use the entire master as an assumed 6 mL dose, or top up an undersized aliquot with DEP. Do not use the old diagnostic Raw/Act microlitre columns for physical dispensing.

Do not spray onto skin, ingest, or evaluate undiluted stocks against the nose. Keep containers away from flames, sparks and heat; work with suitable ventilation and gloves/eye protection selected from the actual supplier SDS. Concentrated ethanol is highly flammable; the cited supplier information is a general handling reference, not proof of your bottle's grade. [Ethanol supplier safety information](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sial/51976)

For the one complete-blend evaluation, use the diluted finished blend on a blotter only after stock-readiness and handling checks. No preliminary comparison formulas are required. If the blend becomes cloudy, separates or forms crystals, pause: apparent clarity does not certify stability, and filtration or extra alcohol would change what is being evaluated. There is no research-established maturation time for Z2; record elapsed time rather than treating a fixed number of days as validation.

## Arithmetic and evidence notes

For each row, supplied product ppm w/w in the 6.500 g concentrate = stock mass g × product mass fraction / 6.500 g × 1,000,000. Example: fresh Coumarin contributes 0.800 × 0.20 = 0.160 g product, or 24,615.38 ppm in the concentrate. This excludes any unassayed coumarin inside Tonkarome.

For a weighed final aliquot and bottle: finished product ppm = concentrate product ppm × transferred concentrate mass / finished solution mass. Actual finished w/w values remain unknown until those masses are measured. The label "96% ethanol" does not establish its w/w-versus-v/v basis.

No threshold crossing or perceptibility is asserted by this card. Existing ODT/OAV screens remain in the [research re-verification](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/a48f/perfume-chem/docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Zero_Astra_Z2_Transition_Research_Reverification_20260906.md), including the unresolved DHBI vapor-pressure discrepancy. No dose was raised in response to that discrepancy; Hexyl Salicylate is described only as a proposed floral modifier, not a verified dry-bark bridge.

Canonical source: [Z2 accounting](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/a48f/perfume-chem/docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Zero_Astra_Z2_accounting.json). This derived recipe preserves all 17 product doses, stock fractions, known carrier totals and the measured-volume finishing definition. The original Z2 formula, old reports, inventory and authority flags are unchanged. New artifact checks do not replace a physical safety or release decision.

